Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:03:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Add MS_GOTLSMLKEM build-time setting

Default tlsmlkem to 0 when MS_GOTLSMLKEM=0 is set while building a program. Preserve explicit module, workspace, source, and runtime GODEBUG overrides. Expose the setting through go env and document its build-time scope.
---
 doc/godebug.md                      | 8 ++++++++
 src/cmd/go/alldocs.go               | 5 +++++
 src/cmd/go/internal/envcmd/env.go   | 3 ++-
 src/cmd/go/internal/help/helpdoc.go | 5 +++++
 src/cmd/go/internal/load/godebug.go | 8 ++++++++
 src/internal/cfg/cfg.go             | 1 +
 6 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/doc/godebug.md b/doc/godebug.md
index ff0c1244e5d0e0a9302de4823f951ca522e23a0a..0e5263c13db172f4868676054e8ed8eb22f2d278 100644
--- a/doc/godebug.md
+++ b/doc/godebug.md
@@ -92,6 +92,14 @@ Because this method of setting GODEBUG defaults was introduced only in Go 1.21,
 programs listing versions of Go earlier than Go 1.20 are configured to match Go 1.20,
 not the older version.
 
+When using the Microsoft build of Go, setting the environment variable
+`MS_GOTLSMLKEM=0` when building a program changes its `tlsmlkem` default to `0`.
+This disables the default use of ML-KEM hybrid TLS groups, including
+X25519MLKEM768. Other values leave the default unchanged. Explicit `godebug`
+and `//go:debug` directives take precedence, and setting `GODEBUG=tlsmlkem=1`
+at runtime re-enables these groups, subject to the other TLS settings.
+Setting `MS_GOTLSMLKEM` only at runtime has no effect.
+
 To override these defaults, starting in Go 1.23, the work module's `go.mod`
 or the workspace's `go.work` can list one or more `godebug` lines:
 
